{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112512","id":2988946927,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6yJ7Xv","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112512","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112512.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112512.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112512","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112512/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112512/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112512/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/068426f10a9be636a9d8879c9ae8296c2813da42","number":112512,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"LSP: Add stdio mode","user":{"login":"pafuent","id":6979945,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5Nzk5NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6979945?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent","html_url":"https://github.com/pafuent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pafuent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes godotengine/godot-proposals#464\r\n\r\nNow Godot can be started as a headless LSP server that reads from stdin and writes to stdout with the `--lsp` CLI parameter.\r\n\r\nBellow is an example of [`helix`](https://helix-editor.com/) using the stdio LSP\r\n\r\n![Helix_Godot_LSP_stdio](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bcd7dac7-eb3b-4b2b-847c-bbf226d0ea41)\r\n\r\n## Helix configuration example\r\n\r\n`helix` configuration to get it working.\r\nLinux and Mac: `~/.config/helix/languages.toml`\r\nWindows: `%AppData%\\helix\\languages.toml`\r\n```toml\r\n[language-server.godot]\r\ncommand = \"<YOUR GODOT BINARY FULL PATH>\"\r\nargs = [ \"--lsp\" ]\r\n\r\n[[language]]\r\nname = \"gdscript\"\r\nlanguage-servers = [ \"godot\" ]\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Testing tool\r\n\r\nIn order to make testing this easier and be sure that having multiple instances of Godot running doesn't broke the project and the LSP works I created a stress testing and validation tool.\r\nIt's spawns multiple concurrent LSP servers and continuously performs various checks to ensure they correctly handles file changes, symbol tracking, and diagnostics.\r\nThe tool does for each LSP server that spawns runs some tests in a forever loop. To prevent issues and because a regular Godot user won't edit code in two different editors at the same time,\r\nthe checks are executed for only one LSP server at a time.\r\nCurrently the checks are (open to write more if makes sense):\r\n- Symbol tracking validation: Adds random functions to GDScript files and verifies the LSP recognizes them\r\n- Diagnostics validation: Creates parent-child class relationships, removes the parent class, and confirms the LSP reports the expected diagnostic error (\"Could not find base class\")\r\nI'm uploading binaries of the tool for Windows, Linux and Mac (I only tested it on Mac, so let me know if you are facing some issue)\r\n\r\nBefore start testing I encourage you to open Godot with the project that you want to test and if it's possible also have open an external editor that connects to Godot LSP Server through TCP (e.g. VSCode)\r\nTo verify that the use of a lot of LSP Servers didn't broke the project you could do a git diff on it or even export it an run it.\r\n\r\n### Usage Example\r\nWe will use Godot 2D platformer demo:\r\n```bash\r\n# Clone the demo project\r\ngit clone https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects\r\ncd godot-demo-projects/2d/platformer\r\n\r\n# Run the test with 3 clients (default)\r\ngodot-lsp-test-os-arch -godot /path/to/godot -project .\r\n\r\n# Run shutdown tests with 3 clients (default)\r\ngodot-lsp-test-os-arch -godot /path/to/godot -project . -test-shutdown\r\n\r\n# Run with 5 clients, checking every 10 seconds, with verbose logging\r\ngodot-lsp-test-os-arch -godot /path/to/godot -project . -clients 5 -interval 10 -verbose\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Binaries (Windows, Linux and Mac)\r\n[godot-lsp-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26649820/godot-lsp-test.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4